  "articles": [
    {
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "3. Confirmation particle ne\n\nThe particle ne at the end of a sentence expresses something like 'aren't you?' or 'isn't it?' in English. Thus, this particle can be used to confirm the name of a person to whom you are introduced. Look at the following example:\n\nYamada-san desu ne?    You're Mr. Yamada, aren't you?\n\nDepending on the pronoun and auxiliary, the confirmation question varies in English, e.g., 'isn't he,' 'don't they,' etc. In Japanese, ne is used no matter what the preceding sentence is."
    }
